// it. The book, editor/docs/oed.nw (an appendix to the C ed's, no "Code
// organization" or "Software architecture" section), gives the design:
// the same backing store as ed (the lines appended to a temporary file,
// zero the array of their offsets, dot and dol the cursors), but the
// input lexed (Lexer.mll, not a source to the map) and parsed by
// peek/consume (Parser, Address) before being run, the globals packed
// in one Env.t, and -r, GNU ed's restricted mode, done by wrapping the
// capabilities (CLI.restrict_caps). The loop: CLI.main, commands (an
// address range parsed and evaluated, a command letter dispatched to
// Commands), global for g/re/cmd running commands again on each marked
// line. The C original is ~/principia/editors/.
